## 36. API/domain normalization boundaries

Pure normalizers accept `unknown`, do not mutate source, reject/skip malformed rows safely, and isolate IDs.

Required normalizers:

- `normalizeBusiness`
- `normalizeService`
- `normalizeDisabledDates`
- `normalizeSlots`
- `normalizeBookingCreateResult`
- `normalizeReservationSummary`
- `normalizeReservationPage`

Leaf UI receives normalized feature-domain values only. API wrappers own raw envelope unwrapping.

## 37. Date/time/timezone contract

- Date is opaque schedule-local `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- Time is opaque `HH:mm`/trimmed `HH:mm:ss`.
- Compare date/time as validated calendar/time parts.
- `addMinutesToTime` computes review-only estimated end without constructing a timezone-bearing date.
- Server `reservationDate`, `startTime`, and `endTime` are authoritative after creation.
- No timezone text, abbreviations, conversions, `UTC`, `店家時間`, or `您的當地時間`.

## 38. Cache/refresh architecture

No global query client.

Reload points:

- Businesses: initial/retry.
- Services + disabled dates: after business selection.
- Slots: after service/date; after conflict.
- Reservation list: initial, filters, sort, page, retry, successful cancellation.
- Filter businesses: initial.
- Filter services: after filter-business change.

State stays feature-local. `AuthContext.refresh()` is not called as a booking/list refresh substitute.

## 39. Accessibility contract

- Exactly one route-level `h1`.
- Logical `h2` section headings.
- Progress has text equivalent and current-step semantics.
- All controls have labels and 44px minimum targets where touch-relevant.
- Flatpickr must be keyboard-operable and validate typed input.
- Slots expose selected/unavailable states beyond color.
- Disabled slot reason is in accessible text.
- Errors are associated using `aria-describedby`.
- Status is icon plus text.
- Mutation feedback is live-region based.
- Reduced-motion preferences disable nonessential transitions.
- Visible focus exists on keyboard interaction; no static arbitrary focus rings.

## 40. Focus-management contract

- Booking initial error retry focuses task heading after successful reload.
- Service error retry returns focus to service section.
- Slot conflict focuses the availability message.
- Dialog/sheet captures opener on open and traps focus.
- Pending confirmation cannot close through Escape/backdrop.
- On normal cancel close, restore opener focus.
- After refresh removes the source action, focus nearest surviving section heading; if none, focus `我的預約` H1.
- After mutation success plus refresh failure, focus stale message/reload control.
- Result state focuses result heading after submit.

## 41. Security/privacy contract

- Render no reservation, user, business IDs, usernames, auth claims, internal timestamps, raw backend messages, or backend DTO dumps.
- Never log booking draft, remark, cancellation reason, CSRF token, or session data.
- Use existing credentialed fetch and CSRF behavior.
- Keep safe internal-only `returnTo`.
- Internal reservation ID exists only in mutation state.
- Ownership remains backend-authoritative.
- Customer route guard is UX/composition protection, not a substitute for backend role authorization.

## 42. Test contract

Future tests must cover:

- Route/guard precedence, anonymous returnTo, customer access, business redirect, no loop, merchant routes unaffected.
- Pure business/service/slot/result/reservation normalizers and malformed payloads.
- Draft invalidation on business/service/date changes.
- Stale preferred-business, service, disabled-date, slot, filter-service, and reservation query responses.
- Booking loading, retry, no services, no slots, unavailable selection, 400, 401, 409, 500, duplicate submit, result, and refresh behavior.
- Local date/time helpers without timezone shifts.
- Sectioning/paging strategy, scheduler-lag records, statuses, filtered/empty/stale state.
- PENDING cancellation, CONFIRMED required reason, duplicate prevention, mutation error, refresh failure, terminal no-action states.
- One H1, accessible progress, slot names/states, dialog/sheet semantics, focus restoration, live feedback.
- Customer shell plus Families 3–6 regression.

No test dependency is added.

## 43. Family 3 regression boundary

