## 49. Known limitations

- Backend has no customer reservation detail endpoint; results cannot survive reload.
- Backend offers generic paged queries only; section grouping is limited to loaded authoritative records.
- Backend lacks business timezone metadata.
- Customer-only frontend routes are not equivalent to backend `ROLE_USER` API authorization.
- Scheduler completion may lag up to five minutes.
- Service selection is backend name-based during creation despite local service ID normalization.

## 50. Unsupported capabilities

Excluded unless backend changes:

- Guest booking
- Staff/provider or any-staff selection
- Price, payment, deposit, receipt, review
- Cancellation policy metadata
- Business timezone claims
- Slot hold, lock, countdown, waitlist
- Reservation detail, reschedule, rebook, edit
- Multiple/recurring/group booking
- Customer chat/messaging

## 51. Remaining open decisions

None blocking Phase 1.

Backend hardening is explicitly deferred:

- Enforce `ROLE_USER` at Family 2 API boundaries.
